 "tile_size_m": 4.0,
 "axes": "Godot: tile centre at the node origin, floor top at y = 0, north = -Z (top of the screen), south = +Z (towards the camera). One MeshLibrary item per shape, built in its base orientation (the sockets below) and turned in the GridMap: every tile is Rotation FourWay. Rotate cells around Y only, never mirror. Each shape is built with its south side open, so a wall or gate turned to the south has the full wall, merlons and arch. Base orientations: room_wall wall on the north, room_corner north and west, room_door outside to the north, corr_bridge* / corr_pad_straight / challenges run north-south, corr_bend opens north and east, corr_pad_bend north and west, corr_pad_t north, south and west.",
 "naming": "Tile names say the godoodungeon tile set: room_* = room tile set (floors, room_wall, room_corner, and room_door = the Door tile), corr_* = corridor tile set (corr_bridge* straights, corr_bend, corr_pad_* bridge pads, corr_chasm* the empty tile, corr_<element>_<challenge> the element challenges of that chamber only). To build a room by hand: room_* tiles only, room_door on the wall ring (not in a corner). room_door_locked = room_door with a doorframe; its door leaves (school_door_leaf.glb) are in its marker scene, which opens them when the door's code is solved.",
 "gridmap_turns": {
  "note": "Quarter turns around +Y as godoowave counts them (counter-clockwise seen from above): the base north side ends up facing the side named here. GridMap cell orientation index per turn.",
